{"seconds": 9.082099792081863, "submission_file": "experiments/generation-extension-v1/submissions/A15/gpt-5-2025-08-07.json", "submission_sha256": "0af4a9ad33b528a7532125234d2ca4aed8245efcdb7050ec4840149134b480c3", "code_sha256": "f290170e3760b86c20d38711d74c41bc9c38d90024e39784e058eb806d5a23cc", "description": "Neuroscience A15 event detector: deterministic per-recording STFT feature extraction with 1 ms hop, 24 log-spaced triangular bands (250\u201312000 Hz), broadband log-energy, and 5/15 ms smoothed broadband features. Noise-floor normalization subtracts each recording\u2019s 20th-percentile log-energy (exact for validation/test, approximate via sparse sampling for non-validation training). A HistGradientBoostingClassifier is trained using up to 60k uniformly sampled frames. Threshold, gap-fill, and minimum-duration hyperparameters are selected by mean event F1 on a fixed validation subset of training recordings, using maximum-cardinality bipartite matching under the specified onset/offset tolerances. The classifier is then refit on all training recordings (re-using computed features where possible), and predictions are post-processed on test recordings to produce 1 ms binary rasters with zeros in padding. Deterministic seeds used; single-thread numeric workload; memory-conscious, streaming per recording.", "code_lines": 422, "line_limit_compliant": false, "line_limit_exclusive": 240}

